                                                                    13 1451
******************************************************************  13 1451
                                                                    13 1451
This evaluation is based on the methodology presented in [1].       13 1451
Path-integral molecular dynamics techniques have been used          13 1451
to produce the input for the neutron scattering model at the        13 1451
indicated temperatures. This includes the radial distribution and   13 1451
velocity autocorrelation functions, which were used to generate     13 1451
the static structure factor and the frequency spectrum. The static  13 1451
structure factor has been used to compute the coherent scattering   13 1451
function with the Skold approximation. For the dynamics, the        13 1451
frequency spectrum was decomposed into solid-like and diffusive     13 1451
parts, which were convoluted with vibrational and rotaional         13 1451
components using previously existing methods [2,3]. This formalism  13 1451
is coded in NJOY-H2D2 [4], which was used to generate the library.  13 1451
                                                                    13 1451
The approach has been benchmarked against previously existing       13 1451
libraries, theoretical calculations and available experimental      13 1451
data in [1].                                                        13 1451
                                                                    13 1451
